            <ArticleTitle>Genetic strategies to understand physiological pathways regulating body weight.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00335-014-9541-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Body weight is a highly heritable trait across species. In humans, genetic variation plays a major role in determining the inter-individual differences in susceptibility or resistance to environmental factors which influence energy intake and expenditure. In this review, I discuss how genetic studies have contributed to our understanding of the central pathways that govern energy homeostasis. The study of individuals harboring highly penetrant genetic variants that disrupt the leptin-melanocortin pathway has informed our understanding of the physiological pathways involved in mammalian energy homeostasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
